    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), derived at read time and recorded at creation.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`mapper/Membership.java`** (new) \u2014 shared helper `levelOf(Owner)`: starts at 1, +1 for a non-blank email, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). Kept as a standalone class so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit mapping method (matching the existing `Locality` pattern).\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `membershipLevel` (via `Membership.levelOf`) instead of `membershipTier`; removed the old `membershipTier` method along with the now-unused `OwnerRepository` field/import (the GOLD-household logic is gone).\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=...` instead of nothing tier-related, alongside the id it already logged.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response property with `membershipLevel` (int32, 1\u20133), which regenerates `OwnerDto` accordingly, removing `membershipTier` from the response.\n\nThe audit output confirms the behavior end-to-end, e.g. `membershipLevel=3` for a unique owner with an email, `membershipLevel=2` for a unique owner without one, and `membershipLevel=1` for a namesake without email.",
